An empty braced-init-list converted to a class type value-initializes the
temporary ([dcl.init.list]/3.5): without a user-provided default constructor
the object is zero-initialized first ([dcl.init.general]/9.1).  In `x = {}'
and in arguments `f({})' the members were left indeterminate.
